cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bow-Grip Biofeedback: An Open Wearable for Measuring Violin Bow-Hold Tension"
message: "If you use this hardware, software, or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sadhukhan
    given-names: Rudra
abstract: >-
  An open-source ESP32-based wearable that continuously measures violin
  bow-grip force, forearm EMG, and bow motion, with optional real-time
  haptic feedback. Includes firmware, logging software, 3D-printable
  enclosure, experimental protocol, pre-registration, analysis code, and
  results of a 33-session single-subject A-B-A-B reversal study.
keywords:
  - biofeedback
  - wearable sensors
  - music performance
  - electromyography
  - playing-related musculoskeletal disorders
  - single-case experimental design
license: MIT
